  "energy_arc": "Intro: slow atmospheric alaap establishing the dark night drone; Mukhada: crushing doom groove enters with the sitar theme; Manjha: brooding drop into the lower mandra register; Mukhada Return: full band locks in heavy reaffirmation; Antara: soaring into the taar register with heightened distortion; Taan: driving virtuosic acceleration to the peak; Mukhada Finale: authoritative resolution on sam; Outro: resonant ring out into subterranean drone.",
  "rhythm_section": {
    "reasoning": "Darbari Kanada doom arrangement plan: In Section 1 (mukhada), establish the primary crushing half-time groove anchored on S power chord (8 beats) driving into g (4 beats) and R (4 beats) with low palm-muted chugs and a 16th-note turnaround resolving onto sam. Sections 3 and 6 replay this exact gat progression via same_as: 1. Section 2 (manjha) shifts into a sparse, subterranean drone floor following S (8 beats) to m (4 beats) and P (4 beats) where power chords ring wide under the sitar's low andolan ornaments. Section 4 (antara) climbs an octave (+1) with soaring distorted sustain over m, P, d, and S (4 beats each) leaving wide space for the taar saptak sitar meends. Section 5 (taan) locks into a relentlessly driving, heavy rhythmic chug pedal on S with brief g and R punctuation to underpin the chaugun lines. Section 7 (outro) strikes a colossal, decaying low tonic power chord ringing out into total darkness.",
